Third-party components
----------------------
Nothing outside this project is distributed with it, so no third-party notice is required for
what Automation Monitor ships and none is claimed here. The Windows package is an explicit
allow-list of the two assemblies this project authors, AutomationMonitor.Plugin.dll and
AutomationMonitor.Core.dll, plus this project's own installer scripts, end-user guide,
manifest and checksum file; and AutomationMonitor.Core references no NuGet package at all.

The plugin is compiled against, and at run time binds to, assemblies the XrmToolBox
installation already supplies. They are recorded here because the rule that keeps them out of
the package is what makes the paragraph above true:

  XrmToolBox and XrmToolBox.Extensibility (NuGet package XrmToolBoxPackage 1.2025.10.74,
    authored by MscrmTools): the XrmToolBox repository is licensed under GNU GPL-3.0, and
    neither its LICENSE.txt nor its README carries a plugin or linking exception; the NuGet
    package itself declares no license metadata. Supplied by the user's XrmToolBox, and not
    distributed here - CopyLocalLockFileAssemblies=false keeps it out of the build output.

  MSCrmTools.Xrm.Connection 1.2025.9.64 (MscrmTools): its package metadata declares
    GNU GPL-3.0 and requireLicenseAcceptance true. Referenced with ExcludeAssets="runtime"
    for compile-time alignment only, and not distributed here.

  Microsoft.Xrm.Sdk and the rest of the Dataverse SDK closure: host-provided, reached through
    the two packages above, and not distributed here.

  Microsoft.NETFramework.ReferenceAssemblies.net48 1.0.3 (Microsoft): a build-only targeting
    pack marked PrivateAssets="all", whose package metadata points at the Microsoft/dotnet
    repository license. It is never linked at run time and never shipped.

  .NET Framework 4.8, Windows Forms and System.Drawing: provided by Windows.

Whether a plugin that links a GPL-3 host assembly forms a derivative work of that host is a
legal question this notice does not answer. It is recorded as an open question in
docs/distribution.md for anyone who redistributes the plugin together with XrmToolBox.
Re-audit this section whenever a PackageReference is added, the packaging allow-list changes,
or a third-party assembly starts shipping with the plugin.
